# Growing two legs: volume and price

The crop growth in the huts has been reduced to two variables:** how much wine (volume)** and ** how much per ton of wine (price)**.

Over the past 10 years (2015-2024), the volume of Mao-Dai liquor sales has increased from approximately 275,000 tons to about 465,000 tons, with annual growth of about ** 5.4 per cent**; the price of the plant has increased from $819 to $1,169 (2023 price increases) and the combined ton price has increased even more (plus structural and direct camp ratios).

** The price was up. What's the future? **

